.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt SSG 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssg
.Nd content directory format for ssg(1)
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A content directory holds a
.Pa site.toml ,
an HTML skeleton, an optional templates directory, markdown pages and any other files.
.Xr ssg 1
turns each page into
.Pa .html ,
.Pa .md
and
.Pa .txt
files in the dist directory and copies everything else.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
site/
  site.toml          configuration
  skeleton.html      HTML around every page
  templates/         for {{extend}} and {{include}}
    base.md
    partials/back.md
  .assetignore       files not to publish
  index.md           -> /
  about.md           -> /about/
  guide/index.md     -> /guide/
  guide/setup.md     -> /guide/setup/
  style.css          copied as is
.Ed
.Sh SITE.TOML
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dist = "dist"                  # required
templates = "templates"        # required
skeleton = "skeleton.html"     # required
base_url = "https://example.com"
clean = true
nested_repos = false
follow_symlinks = false
ignore = ["*.psd", "drafts/"]

[markdown]
html = true
scripts = false
allow_tags = []
allow_attrs = []
heading_ids = true
autolinks = true
extensions = true
text_width = 80
.Ed
.Pp
Relative paths are relative to the content directory.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic dist No (string, required)
Output directory.
It must not be the content directory or contain it, must not contain the templates
directory or the skeleton, and none of its path components below the part it shares with
the content directory may start with
.Sq \&. .
It may be outside the content directory.
.It Ic templates No (string, required)
Templates directory.
It may be missing until a page uses
.Li {{extend}}
or
.Li {{include}} .
Nothing in it is published.
.It Ic skeleton No (string, required)
The HTML skeleton; see
.Sx SKELETON .
Not published.
.It Ic base_url No (string)
Site origin, such as
.Li https://example.com .
Trailing slashes are removed.
When set,
.Pa sitemap.xml
is written; see
.Sx SITEMAP .
.It Ic manifest No (string or false)
Where
.Pa manifest.json
is written, relative to the content directory.
Default: beside
.Ic dist .
.Li false
turns it off.
See
.Sx MANIFEST .
.It Ic clean No (boolean, default true)
Empty dist before building, but only if
.Xr ssg 1
owns it: it holds the
.Pa .ssg-dist
marker, which a build writes into a dist that is missing, empty or already marked.
A non-empty dist without the marker is built over with a warning.
.It Ic future No (boolean, default false)
Build pages whose
.Ic date
is after the build date.
Without it they are held back like drafts.
.It Ic redirect_pages No (boolean, default false)
Also write a meta-refresh page at the old URL of each redirect; see
.Sx REDIRECTS .
.It Ic nested_repos No (boolean, default false)
Also build subdirectories that contain a
.Pa .git
file or directory.
By default they are skipped with a note, so a tool checked out inside the site (for
example by CI) is not published.
.It Ic follow_symlinks No (boolean, default false)
Copy, or render if the name ends in
.Pa .md ,
files that are symbolic links to a file.
By default they are skipped with a note, so a link in untrusted content cannot publish
a file outside the site.
Symbolic links to directories are never followed.
.It Ic ignore No (array of strings)
Patterns in
.Pa .assetignore
syntax, relative to the content directory.
They come before every
.Pa .assetignore
rule, so those can override them.
.El
.Pp
The
.Ic [markdown]
table:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic html No (boolean, default true)
Pass raw HTML through.
False escapes it, so it shows as text.
.It Ic scripts No (boolean, default false)
With
.Ic html
on, false passes raw HTML through an allow-list: only known-harmless tags and attributes
(see
.Ic allow_tags
and
.Ic allow_attrs )
are kept.
Other tags, such as
.Li <script> ,
.Li <iframe> ,
.Li <style> ,
.Li <form> ,
.Li <svg>
and custom elements, are escaped so they show as text; other attributes are dropped, as is
any raw HTML attribute holding a
.Li javascript: ,
.Li vbscript: ,
.Li file:
or non-image
.Li data:
URL.
The same URLs in markdown links and images become
.Li href="#"
or
.Li src="" .
HTML comments are removed.
True turns all of this off and passes everything through.
.It Ic allow_tags No (array of strings)
Extra tag names to allow in raw HTML, for example
.Li ["my-card"] .
.It Ic allow_attrs No (array of strings)
Extra attribute names to allow on any allowed tag, for example
.Li ["style"] .
Event handlers and
.Li srcdoc
are never allowed, and values are still checked for dangerous URLs.
.It Ic heading_ids No (boolean, default true)
Give every heading a GitHub-style id, deduplicated with
.Li -1 ,
.Li -2 ,
\&...
suffixes, unless it sets one with
.Li {#id} .
.It Ic autolinks No (boolean, default true)
GFM bare links:
.Li www.example.com ,
.Li https://example.com ,
.Li user@example.com .
Needs
.Ic extensions .
.It Ic extensions No (boolean, default true)
Everything beyond CommonMark; see
.Sx MARKDOWN .
False gives strict CommonMark syntax.
.It Ic text_width No (integer 0 to 100000, default 80)
Wrap column of the
.Pa .txt
output.
0 disables wrapping.
.El
.Ss The taxonomy tables
A
.Li [taxonomy.tags]
table groups pages by a comma-separated frontmatter value (here
.Ic tags ) .
It generates an index page at
.Pa /tags/
and a page for each term at
.Pa /tags/term/
from
.Pa taxonomy.md
and
.Pa term.md
in the templates directory (a bare list when those are missing).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic key No (string)
The frontmatter key; default the table name.
.It Ic path No (string)
The URL directory; default the table name.
.It Ic title No (string)
The index page's title; default the capitalised name.
.El
.Pp
Both templates see
.Ic taxonomy ,
.Ic taxonomy_title
and
.Ic term_count ;
the index sees
.Ic terms ,
a markdown list of the terms with their page counts; a term page sees
.Ic term ,
.Ic term_slug ,
.Ic term_url ,
.Ic taxonomy_url
and
.Ic pages ,
a markdown list of its pages, newest first.
Every page gets
.Ic tags_links ,
the list of its own terms (named after the table).
.Ss The feed table
The table's presence writes
.Pa feed.xml ,
an Atom 1.0 feed of the dated pages, newest first, with absolute URLs.
It needs
.Ic base_url .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic section No (string)
Only pages under this directory; default every dated page.
.It Ic title No (string)
The feed title; default the host of
.Ic base_url .
.It Ic author No (string)
The feed author; default the title.
.It Ic limit No (integer, default 20)
The number of newest entries kept.
.El
.Pp
Pages with a false
.Ic feed
key and the 404 page are left out.
Entries use the page's
.Ic title ,
.Ic date ,
.Ic description
and
.Ic author .
.Ic feed_url
holds the feed's address while one is written.
A hand-written
.Pa feed.xml
wins, with a warning.
.Ss The robots table
.Pa robots.txt
is written on every build unless the content directory has one.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic enabled No (boolean, default true)
False writes no file.
.It Ic disallow No (array of strings)
Paths, each starting with
.Sq / ,
to disallow for all robots; without any the file says
.Li Allow: / .
.It Ic sitemap No (boolean, default true)
Add a
.Li Sitemap:
line when
.Ic base_url
is set.
.El
.Pp
A hand-written
.Pa robots.txt
wins; with a
.Li [robots]
table present that is a warning.
.Pp
Unknown keys and tables are warnings, not errors.
A key's type must match: a string where a boolean is expected is an error.
.Ss The deploy and headers tables
Hosting adapters, written by
.Nm ssg Cm build
when a target is set (see
.Fl \-target
in
.Xr ssg 1 ) .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic deploy.target No (string)
.Qq cloudflare ,
.Qq vercel
or
.Qq nginx .
.It Ic headers.link No (boolean, default true)
Send a
.Li Link
header with rel=alternate pointing at the Markdown variant of each HTML page.
.It Ic headers.format No (boolean, default true)
Send
.Li X-SSG-Format
(html, md or txt).
.It Ic headers.version No (boolean, default false)
Send
.Li X-SSG-Version .
.It Ic headers.page_cache No (string, default Qq public, max-age=300 )
.Li Cache-Control
for pages; empty sends none.
Fingerprinted files are always immutable.
.El
.Pp
.Li Vary: Accept
and the content type are always sent.
.Ss The css table
CSS is copied as is unless these opt in.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic minify No (boolean, default false)
Minify every
.Pa .css
file before it is published, fingerprinted or inlined: comments (except
.Li /*! ... */ )
are dropped and whitespace is collapsed.
Strings, urls and spaces inside
.Li calc()
are kept.
.It Ic inline_limit No (integer, default 16384)
Warn when a stylesheet embedded with
.Li {{inline}}
is larger than this many bytes; 0 never warns.
.El
.Ss TOML subset
Supported:
.Li #
comments, blank lines,
.Li [table]
headers, bare keys
.Pq Li A-Za-z0-9_-
and quoted keys,
.Li \(dqbasic\(dq
strings with the escapes
.Li \e\(dq \e\e \en \et \er \eb \ef \euXXXX \eUXXXXXXXX ,
.Li \(aqliteral\(aq
strings,
.Li true ,
.Li false ,
integers, and arrays, which may span lines and end with a comma.
A leading UTF-8 BOM and CRLF line endings are accepted.
.Bl -bullet
.It
Dotted keys and headers:
.Li markdown.html = false
is the same as
.Li html = false
under
.Li [markdown] ,
and
.Li [a.b]
is a table inside
.Li a .
Each part is bare or quoted.
A header's parent tables need no header of their own.
.It
Arrays hold any supported value, other arrays included:
.Li [1, [\(dqa\(dq], true] .
Known keys still check their contents:
.Ic ignore
must be an array of strings.
Arrays nest at most 64 deep.
.It
Integers are decimal, with an optional sign, no leading zeros, and
.Sq _
only between two digits, over the full 64-bit range.
.It
Strings are single-line.
Raw control characters other than tab are errors; write them as escapes.
Comments may not hold them either.
.El
.Pp
Not supported, each an error: floats, dates and times, hexadecimal, octal and
binary integers, inline tables, arrays of tables, multi-line strings.
.Pp
Each name is defined once.
These are errors:
.Bl -bullet
.It
a key given twice
.Pq Dq duplicate key \(aqa\(aq ,
or a
.Li [table]
header given twice
.Po
.Dq duplicate table [a] ,
reported on the repeated header's line
.Pc ;
.It
a key that is also a table:
.Dq \(aqa\(aq is not a table ,
.Dq \(aqa\(aq is already a table ,
.Dq table [a] was already defined as a value ;
.It
a table made by dotted keys that later gets a header, or the other way round:
.Dq table [a] was already defined by dotted keys ,
.Dq table [a.b] can't be extended with dotted keys .
.El
.Ss Plugin tables
.Li [plugin.\& Ns Ar name Ns Li \&]
tables declare plugins.
ssg runs
.Pa ssg-plugin- Ns Ar name
(found on
.Ev PATH ,
or at
.Li path )
in the order the tables appear.
.Li enabled ,
.Li path ,
.Li required
(default true) and
.Li timeout
(seconds, default 30) are ssg's own; every other key is the plugin's
configuration, checked against its
.Fl \-meta .
The plugin protocol is frozen from 1.0.0-rc.1; see
.Pa docs/plugins.md
and
.Pa docs/stability.md .
.Li plugin
itself only holds such tables:
.Li plugin = 1
gives
.Dq \(aqplugin\(aq must be a table, like [plugin.<name>] ,
and a key directly in it gives
.Dq [plugin] holds one table per plugin, like [plugin.x] .
.Sh PUBLISHING
The content directory is walked top-down.
.Bl -bullet
.It
Files whose names end in
.Pa .md
are pages.
The match is case-sensitive:
.Pa NOTES.MD
is copied as a file.
.It
Every other regular file is copied to the same path in dist.
Symbolic links to files are copied as files; symbolic links to directories are not
followed.
.It
Names starting with
.Sq \&.
are never published, at any depth, except directories named
.Pa .well-known .
Hidden files inside
.Pa .well-known
are still skipped.
This covers
.Pa .git ,
.Pa .github ,
.Pa .env
and the
.Pa .assetignore
files themselves.
.It
Never published: the dist and templates directories, the skeleton, and
.Pa site.toml
at the top level.
.It
A directory that contains a
.Pa .git
entry is skipped unless
.Ic nested_repos
is true.
.It
A symbolic link to a file is skipped with a note unless
.Ic follow_symlinks
is true.
.It
Paths matched by
.Pa .assetignore
or
.Ic ignore
are skipped, pages included.
.El
.Sh ASSETIGNORE
A
.Pa .assetignore
file may sit in any directory.
Its patterns follow
.Xr gitignore 5
exactly and are relative to that directory:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Blank lines and lines starting with
.Sq #
are ignored;
.Li \e#
starts a pattern with
.Sq # .
.It
.Sq \&!
re-includes what an earlier pattern excluded;
.Li \e!
is a literal
.Sq \&! .
A file cannot be re-included when a parent directory is excluded.
.It
A trailing
.Sq /
matches directories only.
.It
A
.Sq /
at the start or in the middle anchors the pattern to the file's directory; otherwise it
matches a name at any depth below it.
.It
.Sq *
and
.Sq \&?
do not match
.Sq / .
.Li [a-z] ,
.Li [!a-z] ,
.Li [^a-z]
and the ASCII classes
.Li [[:alpha:]] ,
.Li [[:digit:]] ,
etc. match one character.
.Li **/ ,
.Li /**
and
.Li /**/
cross directories.
.Sq \e
escapes the next character.
.It
Trailing spaces are removed unless escaped with
.Sq \e .
.It
Matching is case-sensitive.
A malformed pattern (an unterminated
.Sq \&[ ,
an unknown
.Li [:name:] ,
a trailing lone
.Sq \e )
never matches.
.El
.Pp
Later rules win.
.Ic ignore
patterns come first, then each directory's
.Pa .assetignore ,
parents before children.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# .assetignore for a site deployed with Cloudflare Workers
worker.js
wrangler.jsonc
builder/
.Ed
.Sh OUTPUT
.Bl -column "dir/foo/index.md" "dir/foo/index.{html,md,txt}" "/dir/foo/" -offset indent
.It Sy Source Ta Sy Output Ta Sy URL
.It Pa index.md Ta Pa index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /
.It Pa foo.md Ta Pa foo/index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /foo/
.It Pa dir/index.md Ta Pa dir/index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /dir/
.It Pa dir/foo.md Ta Pa dir/foo/index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /dir/foo/
.El
.Pp
When both
.Pa foo.md
and
.Pa foo/index.md
exist,
.Pa foo.md
is published as
.Pa foo.{html,md,txt}
with the URL
.Pa /foo .
Drafts that are not built do not count.
In URLs, bytes other than
.Li A-Za-z0-9-._~/
are percent-encoded.
.Pp
.Pa .html
is the skeleton with the rendered page in it.
.Pa .md
is the page after templates, includes and the table of contents are resolved, with the
frontmatter removed and leading blank lines dropped.
.Pa .txt
is plain text wrapped at
.Ic text_width .
.Pp
dist also gets
.Pa .ssg-dist ,
a marker that lets later builds empty it, and
.Pa sitemap.xml
when
.Ic base_url
is set.
If two sources write the same file (an asset
.Pa index.html
next to
.Pa index.md ,
say), the page wins and a warning is printed.
.Sh FRONTMATTER
A page or template may start with a block of keys:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
---
title: "Setting up"          # a comment
date: 2024-05-01
order: 2
color: #fff
quote: 'it''s'
empty:
---
.Ed
.Pp
The block starts when the first line is
.Li ---
(blanks around it allowed, after an optional UTF-8 BOM) and ends at the next
.Li ---
line; a missing end is an error.
Inside, each line is blank, a
.Li #
comment, or
.Li key: value .
Keys use
.Li A-Za-z0-9_.- .
Values are strings:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li \(dqdouble\(dq
Everything between the first and the last
.Sq \(dq ,
verbatim: no escapes, so
.Li \(dq$a \eneq b$\(dq
and
.Li \(dqC:\enew\(dq
survive.
A
.Li # comment
may follow the closing quote.
.It Li \(aqsingle\(aq
Literal;
.Li \(aq\(aq
is a quote.
A comment may follow.
.It bare
Trimmed.
A
.Sq #
preceded by a blank starts a comment, so
.Li #fff
is kept.
.Li key:
alone is the empty string.
.El
.Pp
A later key replaces an earlier one.
Line endings may be LF, CRLF or CR.
Values may contain template syntax; it is evaluated like the body.
.Pp
Without a
.Li ---
line, the leading lines of the form
.Li key: \(dqvalue\(dq
(double quotes, ending the line, no comments) are read as keys, up to the first blank or
other line.
This older form exists for compatibility.
.Sh TEMPLATE SYNTAX
Tags are written
.Li {{ ... }} ;
blanks and tabs inside the braces are allowed.
Key names use
.Li A-Za-z0-9_.- ;
.Li else
and
.Li end
are reserved.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li {{key}}
The key's value.
An undefined key stays as written, with inner blanks removed
.Pq Li {{ toc }} No becomes Li {{toc}} .
.It Li {{extend \(dqname\(dq}}
Place this file's body in template
.Ar name
as its
.Li {{content}} .
Only as the first thing in a page or template body (leading blank lines allowed), once;
its line ending goes with it.
Anywhere else it is left as written.
.It Li {{include \(dqname\(dq}}
Insert template
.Ar name
here.
.It Li {{asset \(dqpath\(dq}}
The URL of a copy of the asset
.Ar path
(relative to the content directory) named by a hash of its content, e.g.
.Pa /style.1a2b3c4d5e.css .
The file is also published under its own name.
It is an error if no such asset exists.
.It Li {{inline \(dqpath.css\(dq}}
The text of a stylesheet, for a
.Li <style>
element.
It is an error if the file contains
.Li </style ,
and a warning if it is larger than
.Ic css.inline_limit .
The manifest records a Content-Security-Policy hash of each.
.It Li {{if key}} ... {{else}} ... {{end}}
Keep the first part if
.Ar key
is true, the
.Li {{else}}
part (optional) otherwise.
.It Li {{if not key}}
The same, negated.
.It Li \e{{
A literal
.Li {{ .
.El
.Pp
Text that starts with
.Li {{
but is none of these
.Pq Li {{ foo bar }} , {{}} , {{a:1}}
is left as written.
Template syntax is evaluated everywhere in the page, code blocks and code spans included;
write
.Li \e{{
there to show braces.
.Pp
A template
.Ar name
is a path relative to the templates directory, with
.Pa .md
added unless it ends in
.Pa .md .
Absolute paths,
.Li ..
components and an empty
.Li {{include \(dq\(dq}}
are errors; an empty
.Li {{extend \(dq\(dq}}
is dropped silently and the page is built with no template.
.Pp
A key is true when it is defined and its value, trimmed, is not empty and not
.Li false ,
.Li 0 ,
.Li no
or
.Li off
in any case.
An
.Li {{if}} ,
.Li {{else}}
or
.Li {{end}}
alone on its line (blanks allowed) removes the whole line.
Branches not taken are not evaluated, so an include in one need not exist.
.Li {{if}}
nests up to 256 deep.
.Ss Evaluation
.Bl -enum
.It
The page's frontmatter keys are read and its body kept.
.It
For each
.Li {{extend}}
in the chain, the template's frontmatter keys are added where not already set, and the
template's body, with
.Li {{content}}
set to the body so far, becomes the new body.
.It
Built-in keys are added where not already set.
.It
Every key's value is evaluated, then the body: keys are filled, conditionals and includes
resolved.
Conditionals therefore see the merged keys: a template can test a page key and a page a
template key.
.El
.Pp
Priority is page, then inner template, then outer template, then built-in keys; a page can
override even
.Ic url .
A key that refers to itself through other keys stays as written at the point of the cycle.
Nesting of keys and includes is limited to 64 levels and a result to 64 MiB.
.Pp
An included template's frontmatter keys are defaults for that include only; the
including file's keys win.
One trailing newline is removed from it, so
.Li Hi {{include \(dqname\(dq}}!
stays on one line.
Includes may nest, but may not
.Li {{extend}}
and may not form a cycle.
.Sh BUILT-IN KEYS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic url
The page's URL:
.Li / ,
.Li /guide/ ,
.Li /guide/setup/ .
.It Ic path
Source path relative to the content directory:
.Li guide/setup.md .
.It Ic build_date
.Li YYYY-MM-DD ,
UTC, from
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
when it is set.
.It Ic word_count
Words in the page's plain text, template text included.
A word is a run of non-space bytes with at least one ASCII letter or digit or non-ASCII
byte; each Han, kana or CJK extension character counts as one word of its own.
.It Ic reading_time
Minutes at 200 words or 500 CJK characters a minute, rounded up, at least 1.
.It Ic absolute_url , Ic canonical_url
.Ic base_url
followed by the page URL; defined only when
.Ic base_url
is set.
A page may set
.Ic canonical_url
itself.
.It Ic feed_url
The address of
.Pa feed.xml ,
defined only while a feed is written.
.It Ic og_title
The page's
.Ic title ,
or its navigation title when it has none.
.It Ic og_description
The page's
.Ic description ,
or empty.
.It Ic toc
Table of contents; see
.Sx TABLE OF CONTENTS .
Empty, and so false, when the page has no level 2 to 6 heading.
.It Ic children
The child pages as a markdown list, one
.Li - [Title](/url/)
line each, sorted; empty when there are none.
.It Ic parent_url , Ic parent_title
The parent page.
.It Ic prev_url , Ic prev_title , Ic next_url , Ic next_title
The previous and next sibling, in sorted order.
.El
.Pp
The parent and sibling keys are not defined when there is no such page, so they stay as
written; test them with
.Li {{if prev_url}} .
While the first pass runs, all navigation keys,
.Ic toc ,
.Ic word_count
and
.Ic reading_time
are empty.
.Ss Keys with a meaning
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic title
Fills the skeleton's
.Li <title> .
.It Ic nav_title , Ic page_title , Ic title
The first that is not blank is the page's title in
.Ic children ,
.Ic parent_title ,
.Ic prev_title
and
.Ic next_title .
Without any, the file name without
.Pa .md ,
or the directory name for an
.Pa index.md .
.It Ic order
A number; see
.Sx NAVIGATION .
.It Ic date
Sort key, compared as a string, so use
.Li YYYY-MM-DD .
Also the sitemap's
.Li <lastmod> .
.It Ic draft
When true, the page is built only with
.Fl \-drafts .
It may be set by a template.
.It Ic sitemap
When defined and false, the page is left out of
.Pa sitemap.xml .
.It Ic noindex
When true, the page is left out of
.Pa sitemap.xml .
.It Ic content
Set by
.Li {{extend}} ;
in the skeleton, the page's HTML.
.El
.Sh NAVIGATION
The parent of
.Pa dir/foo.md
is
.Pa dir/index.md ;
the parent of
.Pa dir/index.md
is the
.Pa index.md
one directory up.
Top-level pages have the root
.Pa index.md
as parent; it has none.
A page whose parent file does not exist has no parent and no siblings.
Siblings are the parent's children.
.Pp
Children are sorted by:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Ic order ,
ascending; pages with a numeric
.Ic order
come first.
It is read as a floating-point number; anything else, including
.Li nan ,
counts as no order.
.It
.Ic date ,
ascending as a string; dated pages come first.
.It
source path.
.El
.Sh TABLE OF CONTENTS
In a page or template,
.Li {{toc}}
becomes a markdown list of the page's level 2 to 6 headings, nested by level relative to
the shallowest, each linking to the heading's id.
It is put on lines of its own with blank lines around, so it should stand on a line of
its own (not inside a list or quote).
In the skeleton,
.Li {{toc}}
is the same list as HTML.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{{if toc}}
**Contents**

{{toc}}
{{end}}
.Ed
.Sh SKELETON
One HTML file wraps every page.
.Bl -bullet
.It
The page's HTML replaces whatever is inside the first
.Li <main ...>
\&...
.Li </main>
(case-insensitive), or goes where
.Li {{content}}
is if the skeleton has one.
Without either, the build fails.
.It
If the page has a
.Ic title
key, its value, HTML-escaped, replaces the text inside the first
.Li <title> ;
otherwise the skeleton's own text stays.
.It
.Li {{key}}
is any of the page's keys after evaluation, built-in keys included, HTML-escaped
.Pq Li & < > \(dq \(aq .
.Li {{content}}
and
.Li {{toc}}
are inserted as HTML.
.It
.Li {{if}} ,
.Li {{if not}} ,
.Li {{else}} ,
.Li {{end}}
and
.Li \e{{
work as in templates; unbalanced conditionals are an error.
.Li {{include}} ,
.Li {{extend}}
and undefined keys are left as written.
.El
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>My site</title>
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://example.com{{url}}">
</head>
<body>
{{if draft}}<p class="draft">Draft</p>{{end}}
<main>
</main>
<footer>Built {{build_date}}.</footer>
</body>
</html>
.Ed
.Sh MARKDOWN
CommonMark 0.31.2 (all 652 spec examples pass), plus, unless
.Ic extensions
is false:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
GFM tables (a delimiter row with
.Sq | ;
.Li \e|
in a cell is a literal pipe), task lists
.Li - [x] ,
strikethrough
.Li ~x~
and
.Li ~~x~~ ,
bare autolinks.
.It
footnotes
.Li [^label]
with
.Li [^label]: text ,
and inline
.Li ^[text] .
.It
definition lists: a term line, then
.Li ": definition" .
.It
alerts
.Li > [!NOTE] ,
.Li [!TIP] ,
.Li [!IMPORTANT] ,
.Li [!WARNING] ,
.Li [!CAUTION] .
.It
containers
.Li ::: name Optional title
\&...
.Li ::: ,
rendered as
.Li <div class="alert name"> .
.It
.Li ==mark== .
.It
heading attributes
.Li ## Title {#id .class} .
.El
.Pp
Raw HTML, heading ids and the sanitizer are set by the
.Ic [markdown]
table.
The
.Pa .txt
output renders the same tree as plain text: setext-style underlined headings, links as
.Li text <url> ,
lists and tables laid out, wide characters counted as two columns.
.Sh DATA FILES
Files named
.Pa *.toml
or
.Pa *.json
directly inside
.Pa data/
in the content directory are not published.
They are read before the build and flattened into keys prefixed with the file name:
.Pa data/site.toml
holding
.Li author = "Ann"
gives
.Li {{data.site.author}} .
Tables and objects nest with a dot.
Array items are numbered
.Pq Li data.site.tags.0
and the array's size is
.Li data.site.tags.length .
Booleans are
.Li true
or
.Li false ,
numbers keep their text and JSON
.Li null
is empty.
Data has the lowest priority, so a page's frontmatter can override it.
Invalid data stops the build.
.Sh PAGINATION
.Li paginate: "N"
in the frontmatter of an
.Pa index.md
shows N children per page.
The index page is page 1; further pages are generated at
.Pa page/2/ ,
.Pa page/3/
and so on below its directory, from the same source.
Each page's
.Ic children
holds its own slice.
.Ic page_number
and
.Ic page_count
number the pages;
.Ic prev_page_url
and
.Ic next_page_url
are empty at the ends.
A value that is not a whole number from 1 to 100000, or a page that is not an
.Pa index.md ,
is ignored with a warning.
.Sh REDIRECTS
.Pa redirects.txt
in the content directory is not published.
Each line is
.Ar from to Op Ar status ;
blank lines and
.Sq #
comments are ignored.
.Ar from
starts with
.Sq / ,
.Ar to
is a path starting with
.Sq /
or an http(s) URL, and
.Ar status
is 301 (the default), 302, 303, 307 or 308.
Bad lines and repeated sources are skipped with a warning.
The rules are written to
.Pa _redirects
(one
.Ar from to status
line each, as Cloudflare Pages and Netlify read it) and to the
.Li redirects
array of the manifest.
A
.Pa _redirects
in the content directory wins, with a warning.
With
.Li redirect_pages = true
in
.Pa site.toml ,
rules without a wildcard also get a page with a meta refresh at the old URL.
.Sh SITEMAP
With
.Ic base_url
set,
.Pa sitemap.xml
lists every built page, sorted by URL, as
.Li <loc>
holding
.Ic base_url
followed by the page URL, plus
.Li <lastmod>
when
.Ic date
starts with
.Li YYYY-MM-DD
(alone or followed by
.Sq T
or a blank).
Pages with a false
.Ic sitemap
key, a true
.Ic noindex
key, and the
.Li 404
page are left out.
A
.Pa sitemap.xml
in the content directory is copied instead, with a warning.
.Sh MANIFEST
Every build writes
.Pa manifest.json
beside
.Ic dist ,
never inside it, so it is not deployed.
It is a JSON object with
.Li schema
(1; fields are only added within a schema),
.Li ssg_version ,
.Li build_date
(honours
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH ) ,
.Li base_url ,
.Li pages ,
.Li assets ,
.Li inline_styles ,
.Li redirects
and
.Li plugins .
Each page has
.Li url ,
.Li source ,
.Li title ,
.Li date
and
.Li outputs ,
three objects with
.Li path ,
.Li format
.Pq html , md , txt
and
.Li content_type .
Each asset has
.Li path ,
.Li output
and
.Li size ;
one used through
.Li {{asset}}
also has
.Li fingerprint ,
.Li fingerprint_size
and
.Li immutable .
.Li inline_styles
lists each
.Li {{inline}}d
stylesheet with
.Li path ,
.Li size
and
.Li csp_hash
.Pq Li sha256-... .
A file that exists at the target and was not written by
.Xr ssg 1
is left alone with a warning.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A series: a section index and two posts that share a layout.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
==> templates/base.md <==
# {{page_title}}

{{content}}

==> templates/post.md <==
---
page_title: "{{series}}: {{title}}"
---
{{extend "base"}}
{{content}}

{{if prev_url}}Previous: [{{prev_title}}]({{prev_url}}){{end}}
{{if next_url}}Next: [{{next_title}}]({{next_url}}){{end}}

{{include "partials/back"}}

==> templates/partials/back.md <==
Back to [{{parent_title}}]({{parent_url}}).

==> guide/index.md <==
---
title: "Guide"
---
{{children}}

==> guide/setup.md <==
---
title: "Setup"
series: "Guide"
order: 1
---
{{extend "post"}}
Install it.

==> guide/usage.md <==
---
title: "Usage"
series: "Guide"
order: 2
---
{{extend "post"}}
Use it.
.Ed
.Pp
.Pa dist/guide/setup/index.md
comes out as:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Guide: Setup

Install it.



Next: [Guide: Usage](/guide/usage/)

Back to [Guide](/guide/).
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Li {{if prev_url}} ... {{end}}
line is not a standalone tag, so when false it leaves an empty line; markdown ignores it.
.Pa /guide/
lists both posts as
.Li - [Guide: Setup](/guide/setup/)
and
.Li - [Guide: Usage](/guide/usage/) :
.Ic page_title
comes before
.Ic title
for link titles.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssg 1 ,
.Xr gitignore 5
